Interview Answer (2-Minute Version)

"I would design the notification system using an event-driven architecture. Business services such as Order Service or Payment Service publish notification events to Kafka. A Notification Service consumes these events, checks user preferences, resolves templates, and routes notifications to Email, SMS, Push, or In-App channels. Each channel has dedicated consumers for independent scaling. Failed deliveries are retried using Spring Retry and moved to a DLQ after max retry attempts. Idempotency is ensured using a unique notification ID. Redis-based rate limiting protects third-party providers. Kafka consumer groups allow horizontal scaling, while provider failover ensures high availability. Metrics are collected through Prometheus and Grafana for monitoring."

This is typically the level expected from a senior backend engineer/system design interview.

